    "chapter_name": "Ray Optics",
    "year": "2023",
    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A monochromatic light wave with wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in air enters another medium. If the angle of incidence and angle of refraction at the interface are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> respectively, then the wavelength&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;of the refracted wave are:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>By using Snell&#39;s law,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, the refractive index is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Also using the relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mi>v</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is the refractive index,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is the velocity of light in air&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>&nbsp;is the velocity in the medium</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mtext>air&#160;</mtext></msub><mrow><mtext>v</mtext><mtext>&#160;</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mtext>1&#160;</mtext></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>The velocities&nbsp;are&nbsp;given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#957;</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#957;</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>The frequency of light does not change when the medium changes.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}